[題目]  
In MongoDB document modeling, one-to-one relationships can be represented using embedding or referencing. A developer is designing a system where each 'user' document has a corresponding 'passport' document. The passport data is accessed every time the user logs in (alongside user data), is never shared across multiple users, and each user has exactly one passport. However, the passport subdocument contains a large number of fields that frequently change independently (visa stamps, expiry updates, renewal status). Which consideration most strongly argues AGAINST embedding the passport subdocument directly inside the user document? (difficulty: hard)
在 MongoDB 文件建模中，一對一關係可以透過內嵌或引用來表示。開發者正在設計一個系統，每個「使用者 (user)」文件都有一個對應的「護照 (passport)」文件。護照資料每次使用者登入時都會（與使用者資料一起）被讀取，絕不跨使用者共享，且每個使用者恰好擁有一本護照。然而，護照子文件包含大量頻繁獨立變更的欄位（簽證蓋章、過期更新、換發狀態）。哪項考量最強烈地「反對」將護照子文件直接內嵌於使用者文件中？（難度：高）

[選項]  
A. MongoDB does not support subdocument updates, so embedding would make passport field updates impossible.
B. Frequent independent updates to the embedded subdocument cause the entire parent document to be rewritten on each change, increasing write amplification and potential document fragmentation.
C. Referencing is always preferred over embedding in one-to-one relationships because it avoids data duplication between collections.
D. Embedding a subdocument with many fields will always exceed MongoDB's 16MB document size limit, making referencing mandatory.

[正確答案]：
B

[核心考點]： 

[詳細解析]：
當內嵌子文件經常獨立更新且大小改變時，會導致父文件在硬碟上頻繁重新分配空間與寫入，造成寫入放大（Write Amplification）與碎片化問題。

A. 錯誤，MongoDB 完全支援對子文件欄位進行更新（如點號表示法 `$set: { "passport.expiry": ... }`）。
B. 正確，頻繁變動子文件會引發文件尺寸改變，進而導致磁碟重新分配空間與寫入放大。
C. 錯誤，一對一關係通常優先推薦「內嵌」而非引用，選項敘述不正確。
D. 錯誤，護照資料通常僅幾 KB，絕不可能單純因欄位較多就超過 16MB 限制。

