[題目]  
In MongoDB document modeling, one-to-one relationships can be represented either by embedding a subdocument or by using a reference (storing an ObjectId pointing to a separate collection). A developer is building a system where each 'employee' document has a corresponding 'employeeProfile' containing detailed biographical data (large text fields, rarely accessed). The employee collection is queried frequently for basic info (name, department, role), while the profile data is fetched only occasionally. The profile data is never shared across multiple employee documents, and each employee always has exactly one profile. Which modeling approach best fits this scenario and why? (difficulty: medium)
在 MongoDB 文件建模中，一對一關係可以透過內嵌子文件或使用引用（儲存指向獨立集合的 ObjectId）來表示。開發者正在建置一個系統，其中每個「員工 (employee)」文件都有一個對應的「員工個人檔案 (employeeProfile)」，包含詳細的生平資料（大型文字欄位、極少被存取）。員工集合經常被查詢基本資訊（姓名、部門、角色），而個人檔案資料僅偶爾被擷取。個人檔案資料絕不跨多個員工文件共享，且每個員工恰好有一個個人檔案。哪種建模方法最適合此情境且原因為何？（難度：中等）

[選項]  
A. Embed the employeeProfile subdocument inside the employee document, because one-to-one relationships in MongoDB must always be modeled with embedding to avoid application-level joins.
B. Store the employee data inside the employeeProfile document as a nested subdocument, reversing the ownership, because MongoDB performance is always better when the larger document owns the smaller one.
C. Use a reference - store an ObjectId in the employee document pointing to a separate employeeProfile collection, because the profile data is large and infrequently accessed, keeping the employee documents lean for common queries.
D. Embed the employeeProfile subdocument inside the employee document, because embedding always provides the best read performance regardless of access patterns.

[正確答案]：
C

[核心考點]： 

[詳細解析]：
將大體積且罕用資料拆至獨立集合（引用模式），能精簡頻繁查詢的主文件大小，減少記憶體（RAM）與 I/O 消耗。

A. 錯誤，一對一關係非強制內嵌，需視存取模式（Access Patterns）彈性選擇。
B. 錯誤，反轉所有權與效能無關，且無法解決主文件查詢體積過大的問題。
C. 正確，採引用分離大體積罕用資料，可使高頻查詢的主文件保持精簡高效。
D. 錯誤，忽視存取模式直接內嵌，會導致高頻查詢無謂載入不必要的大量欄位。

